BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coding with Python IV
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T190000
UID:6a1e0f19c7d3cd58005d5efb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this follow up course we will be looking into the next stag
 es of error handling (including making some custom error messages).\nPytho
 n is an open source programming language that is used for creating web app
 lications\, web content\, mathematics and system scripting. In this follow
  up course we will take our understanding of data structures to the next l
 evel as well as looking into the next stages of error handling (including 
 making some custom error messages) and extending our knowledge of input/ou
 tput to more than just the terminal.\nThis class is for beginners but assu
 mes you have a basic understanding of Python or have attended Coding with 
 Python I\, II\, and III.\nPrior to the class\, participants will need to d
 ownload and install Python and VS Code onto their personal computers (inst
 allation guides provided after registration).\nRegistration is limited and
  specific instructions including information about software installation w
 ill be provided.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information
  on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public 
 Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will o
 nly be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. 
 Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed t
 o Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Stre
 et\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, 2nd Floor Learning Center
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1e0f19c7d3cd58005d5efb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Art by Kazui Ikenshi
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T090000
UID:6a24322a7b73be6a1b1ab8f4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, works by artist Kazui Ikenishi
  are on display at Bloor Gladstone Library in an exhibit.\nKazui Ikenishi 
 is an abstract painter born and raised in Japan\, now based in Toronto\, C
 anada. A self-taught artist\, she began painting in September 2023 and qu
 ickly developed a passion for vibrant\, expressive compositions. Working p
 rimarily with acrylic paint\, she embraces bold colors and dynamic forms 
 in her artwork. Her creative process is deeply intuitive\, often drawing i
 nspiration from her own sketches and spontaneous explorations on the\ncanv
 as.\nKazui's works explores spontaneity\, movement\, and connection throu
 gh bold colors and fluid forms. Starting with rough underdrawing on a read
 ymade canvas\, she let's intuition guide the composition.  Using opaque a
 crylics\, she creates a rhythm - flowly like music- where shapes interact 
 freely\, much like an improvisational melody.  The overlapping colors and
  organic forms symbolize how elements in life connect.  She balances stru
 cture and spontianeity\, allowing each piece to evolve naturally.\nThe exh
 ibit can be viewed during Bloor/Gladstone branch's open hours. Please che
 ck the\nBloor/Gladstone branch\npage before you visit.\nFree. All are welc
 ome.\nImage credit: Kazui Ikenshi\; Infinite Connection\; Medium: Acrylic
LOCATION:Bloor/Gladstone\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a24322a7b73be6a1b1ab8f4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
