BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coding with Python V
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T200000
UID:69fa1b8ce8af4a2f0070520f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this follow up course we will be looking into the next stag
 es of error handling (including making some custom error messages).\nPytho
 n is an open source programming language that is used for creating web app
 lications\, web content\, mathematics and system scripting. In this follow
  up course we will take a break from the logical side of back-end developm
 ent and get our feet wet with a little bit of front-end coding\; we'll mak
 e a user interface! Using tkinter\, a popular module for creating user-fac
 ing layouts\, we will design and implement a simple but effective UI for o
 ur Python code. This will allow us to run our programs using another platf
 orm other than Terminal.\nThis class is for beginners but assumes you have
  a basic understanding of Python or have attended Coding with Python I\, I
 I\, III\, and IV.\nPrior to the class\, participants will need to download
  and install Python and VS Code onto their personal computers (installatio
 n guides provided after registration).\nRegistration is limited and specif
 ic instructions including information about software installation will be 
 provided.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on thi
 s form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librari
 es Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be 
 used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questio
 ns about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answe
 rline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, To
 ronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fa1b8ce8af4a2f0070520f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bead Art Painting Workshop- Inspired by Métis Floral Beadwork
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T200000
UID:6a10913c8360de907d880e09@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Discover what makes Métis beadwork unique and create your own
  work of art!\nIn this workshop\, participants will learn about the histor
 y of Métis beadwork and the symbolism behind each bead used. Attendees wi
 ll discover how historical beadwork patterns led to a new form of pointill
 ism\, where every dot of paint represents a bead. Participants will explor
 e this contemporary art form by creating their own bead art painting to ta
 ke home. No experience needed.\nSpace is limited. Registration required.\n
 Marissa Magneson is a Cree-Métis artist\, photographer\, and educator wit
 h Red River roots\, She holds a BFA (Hons.) and a Master’s in Indigenous
  Studies with a focus on beadwork as visual storytelling. Her work centers
  on decolonizing education\, community strengthening\, and reclaiming cult
 ural practices\, and she has been nationally recognized as a 2023 Vanier S
 cholar and one of York University’s Top 30 Alumni Under 30. Currently a 
 PhD candidate at York University researching ‘Beadwork as Pedagogy’\, 
 Marissa also teaches\, creates\, and facilitates workshops. She is inspire
 d by the legacy of her Métis grandmother\, Elaine Jessop (Desjarlais).\nI
 nformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is co
 llected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sec
 tions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for eve
 nt and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how
  the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff 
 at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a10913c8360de907d880e09
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Meditative Art by Izabella Lipowski
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T235959
UID:6a1af88fc6a1dc3d00d72df1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June the works of Izabella Lipowski ar
 e on display at Morningside branch\nIzabella is a self - taught artist and
  retired Community Support Worker who was lucky to merge her formal educat
 ion with her love of art. During her working years she taught various cra
 fts (weaving\, paper work\, jewelry making) as well as drawing and paintin
 g in different mediums to adults with special needs\, encouraging their c
 reativity. Her favourite subject and biggest inspiration is drawn from the
  plant world and her favourite medium is\nwatercolours\, but also experime
 nts with mixed media.\nIzabella believes that anyone has the ability to ma
 ke art. She believes that many times focusing on producing “masterpieces
 ” stays in the way of our creativity. For her\, non - representational\,
  abstract drawing could be a way to let ourselves be curious\, spontaneous
  and playful. Her hope is that the viewers feel encouraged to give it a tr
 y themselves.\nThis exhibit is part of\nTPL's Art Exhibit\nprogram. Toront
 o Public Library provides space for local artists to exhibit their work at
  locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cult
 ural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be vie
 wed during Morningside branch open hours. Please check the\nMorningside br
 anch\npage before your visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Title
  of Piece: Together Medium (e.g. oil\, acrylic\, photography\, etc.): pens
  & metallic pencils Size/Dimensions: Small
LOCATION:Morningside
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1af88fc6a1dc3d00d72df1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
