BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pride Movie Night: The Haunting (1963)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T193000
UID:6a245a7b43b41b3d006c4614@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Cap off your Pride Month celebrations with a historically inf
 luential 2SLGBTQ+ horror movie!\nThe atmospheric horror movie\nThe Haunti
 ng\n(1963)\n\, interpreting the novel\nThe Haunting of Hill House\n(1959) 
 by Shirley Jackson\, depicts a paranormal researcher and three others he s
 elects to investigate an apparently haunted house.\nProduced at the end of
  the Hays Code era\, when 2SLGBTQ+ storylines were de-facto banned\, this
  movie is nevertheless known for its subtle depiction of a lesbian charact
 er and the intimation of a relationship between the characters Theodora (C
 laire Bloom) and Eleanor (Julie Harris)\, as they try to survive with thei
 r sanity intact.\nThe Haunting\nhas been rated G\, PG\, and 14A. Content w
 arnings: death\, suicide\, psychosis\, vehicular accidents\, implications
  of elder neglect and harm to children.\nRefreshments will be provided and
  ingredients lists will be available.\nDrop-in space is available until ro
 om capacity is reached.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a245a7b43b41b3d006c4614
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
