BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Woven Wonders: Inside a Bird's Nest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260715T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260715T200000
UID:6a3312a7f56bd86e00b76feb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A bird’s nest is its home. Or is it?\nWhy and how do birds b
 uild nests\, and most importantly\, why do some birds’ nests seem less s
 ophisticated than others?\nLet’s look at the many ways birds build nests
 \, from elaborate cup nests and cavity nests to seemingly random spots on 
 an open roof\, and places so secretive you wouldn’t even know a bird was
  living there! Learn how nesting habitat matters to birds and how you can
  protect their homes and help them thrive.\nPresented by the Toronto and R
 egion Conservation Authority (TRCA) as part of TPL’s environmental progr
 am series\,\nOur Fragile Planet\n. Photo provided by TRCA. Drop-in\, no re
 gistration required.\nIf you would like to receive a reminder email/call 
 before the event\, please click the "register" button to provide us with 
 your contact information.\n= = = = =\nAbout the presenter:\nShane Aberneth
 y is the Bander-in-Charge at the Tommy Thompson Park Bird Research Station
  and host of the TRCA's Feathered Friday social media series. He has studi
 ed birds for the past eight years and birded across the country. His favou
 rite bird is the American Kestrel.
LOCATION:Danforth/Coxwell\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3312a7f56bd86e00b76feb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
