DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T140000
UID:6a2ef263414ef43d0096d7e9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an interactive discussion with Career Coach in Res
 idence Sangeetha Dikshit and guest speaker\, Abirambika Ravivarman. Resili
 ence is more than bouncing back\, it's our capacity to navigate change\, u
 ncertainty\, and challenges with greater awareness\, adaptability\, and pu
 rpose. In this interactive session\, participants will explore the concept
  of Resilient Flow and how our beliefs\, habits\, and ways of making sense
  of the world influence how we respond under pressure.\nAbirambika Ravivar
 man\nis a Human-Centric Leadership and Systems Coach and the founder of Hu
 man Systems at Work.\nSangeetha Dikshit\n\, one of TPL's three Spring 2026
  Career Coaches in Residence. Sangeetha is a Career and Leadership Coach 
 empowering individuals to navigate career transitions\, develop in-demand 
 skills\, and achieve professional success.\nThis program is part of TPL's 
 Career Coaches in Residence and is generously supported by our lead donor 
 Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors Fidelity Canada\, Friends 
 of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter and\nWilliam and Nona Heaslip Fo
 undation.\nFor more information\, please visit\ntpl.ca/careercoach
