BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Using Labour Market Information to Make Career Decisions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T140000
UID:6a3c17d286636e3d00505011@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Finding the right labour market information (LMI) for your job
  search can be complex\, especially when you’re trying to figure out whi
 ch jobs are growing\, what skills employers are asking for\, or where to s
 tart your search.\nJoin one of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence\, Shene
 lle Payne Cuffy and an expert from the Labour Market Information Council
  will introduce two free tools from the LMIC\, the Canadian Job Trends D
 ashboard and the Youth Employment Dashboard.\nAbout the Labour Market Info
 rmation Council (LMIC)\nLMIC was created to address long-standing challeng
 es in Canada’s labour market information (LMI) ecosystem. LMIC works to 
 improve the timeliness\, reliability\, and accessibility of labour market 
 information across jurisdictions.\nThis program is part of TPL's Career Co
 aches in Residence and is generously supported by our lead donor Azrieli F
 oundation along with supporting donors Fidelity Canada\, Friends of Toront
 o Public Library\, South Chapter and William and Nona Heaslip Foundation.\
 nFor more information\, please visit\ntpl.ca/careercoach
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3c17d286636e3d00505011
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
