BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Protecting Your Family Treasures
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T153000
UID:6a25d2f04407827f8aa33c21@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Many of us have treasured items - such as books\, photographs\
 , letters\, and documents - that reflect our family histories and hold dee
 p personal significance. Beyond their sentimental value\, these materials 
 also form an important part of our shared cultural heritage. Over time\, h
 owever\, such items can become fragile and vulnerable to damage\, making p
 roper care essential to preserve them for future generations.\nJoin conser
 vator Andrew Huot for an engaging and informative session on how to care f
 or your family treasures. Learn practical and effective methods for preser
 ving\, protecting\, and safely storing these meaningful items\, ensuring t
 hey can be enjoyed and appreciated for years to come.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a25d2f04407827f8aa33c21
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
