SUMMARY:Understanding Credit and Fraud Protection
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T153000
UID:6a3466bf43b41b3d006f7fde@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Presented by\nWest Neighbourhood House\n\, this session will h
 elp participants understand basic credit principles. They will learn how t
 o differentiate between a credit score and a credit report and recognize t
 he roles of Canada’s two major credit bureaus. The session will also dis
 cuss interest rates\, responsible credit card use\, predatory lending tact
 ics\, and fraud protection.\nDrop in\, no registration required.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
