BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Secrets of Rosehill Reservoir
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T193000
UID:6a2d581ecaf934360062d19f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Rosehill Reservoir and David A. Balfour Park are the largest g
 reen spaces in midtown Toronto. Join photojournalist Ian Darragh for an il
 lustrated talk celebrating this much-loved park.\nYou will learn about the
  many environmental benefits of urban parks\; Toronto’s unique ravines\;
  local history\, and how Rosehill Reservoir is a key component of Toronto
 ’s pioneering public drinking water system which saved thousands of chil
 dren from outbreaks of typhoid and other waterborne diseases.\nIan Darragh
  is a former editor-in-chief of Canadian Geographic and writer for Nationa
 l Geographic. He contributed\ntwo feature articles\nabout\nRosehill Reserv
 oir\nand David A. Balfour Park in\nSpacing magazine\n.
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Upstairs in room 204
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2d581ecaf934360062d19f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
